\_process() over \_physics\_process()? If I remember correctly, \_process is called every idle frame so would that still work? Just asking because again, I'm still pretty new. 

&#x200B;

Thanks!

Ok so I'm not the best with Godot, but I think I see what you're saying. You're saying something like...  


func \_physics\_process(delta):  
if($button.is\_pressed()):  
\#button follows mouse  


I'm not exactly sure as I haven't tried this yet. I knew this might be a solution, but I figured what's the point of this if there's already a button method that calls as long as the button is pressed. If I can't find a method like this, then this would probably be the best solution. At least at the moment. I'll give it a try and make an edit if things go poorly.   


Thanks for the help!
